{
  "text": "On this day, September 13th: In 2007: The McLaren F1 team are found guilty of possessing confidential information from the Ferrari team, fined $100 million, and excluded from the constructors' championship standings. In 1993: Nirvana released their third and final studio album, In Utero, which went on to sell more than 15 million copies. And in 1985: Super Mario Bros., one of the most influential and best-selling video games in history, was first released in Japan for the Nintendo Entertainment System.",
